recommend check-in (Keaton) -- one seat is new and two stand. NEW: the enclosure read-only-maps the host's whole /sys and read-write-binds the host X11 socket directory, and Pond's record now refuses both out loud; four mask lines close the classic corners under that /sys map, and teaching the reading to weigh a mask against the map above it would be a real improvement AND a loosening of an isolation boundary, which the quest puts at check-in rather than in the lap that found it. STANDING: the REDS pin at 24,571 of 24,576 with every row OPEN, which refused %335 and refuses these three -- one word either folds an OPEN row or raises living_pin_max_bytes for that one page, as was done once for the session-logs pin; and this pier's own enclosure.conf, still pinning two elders under %327. Mechanically the next Hush lap is orbit two's grants themselves, now derivable from a record that names the whole enclosure rather than a sixth of it -- and it brushes Dream's lane at Caravan's capability pieces, so it wants his nod first.
